# 11 Nov 2026. A light space's tips are light (TooltipTones.forSpace). A plain click on a tab, or a
# click on the list's empty space, clears a ⌘-click selection. A tab still loading off screen spins an
# arc round its favicon (TabLoadingIndicator), and the tab on screen doesn't (it has the loading bar).
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
wait 2
cra://debug?tooltip=Hello
wait 0.5
expect-log tooltip shown: light
# ${STALL} never answers: its tab keeps loading once another tab is in front.
cra://open?url=${STALL}/slow
wait 1.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=front
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1.5
cra://debug?loadingRows=background
expect-log loading rows background: 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=third
wait 1.5
# Picks: ⌘-click two rows, then a plain click on one leaves none picked.
cra://debug?pickTabs=0,1
cra://debug?picksState=picked
expect-log tab picks picked: [2-9]
cra://debug?plainClickTab=0
cra://debug?picksState=afterClick
expect-log tab picks afterClick: 0
# Picks again, then a click on the list's empty space.
cra://debug?pickTabs=0,1
cra://debug?emptyListClick=1
expect-log tab picks cleared: a click on the list's empty space
cra://debug?picksState=afterEmpty
expect-log tab picks afterEmpty: 0
# A plain click anywhere in the sidebar that isn't a row, tile, button or control clears the picks
# too: the space's header here. A tab row's own click is the row's (it selects just that tab).
cra://debug?pickTabs=0,1
cra://debug?sidebarClick=TabRowView,0
expect-log sidebar click TabRowView,0: picks kept
cra://debug?sidebarClick=SpaceHeaderView
expect-log sidebar click SpaceHeaderView: picks cleared
cra://debug?picksState=afterHeader
expect-log tab picks afterHeader: 0
